# Copy to local.env (gitignored — never commit real paths) and fill in.
# local.env is sourced automatically by bin/leakage-audit.
#
# TIP: to validate without any private installation, skip this file and
# point at the bundled synthetic stub instead:
#   export PERSONAL_MEMORY_SKILL="$PWD/test/stub-memory-skill"
#   export MOCHI_AGENTS_FILE="$PWD/test/stub-memory-skill/AGENTS.md"
# The stub is a test double for harness self-consistency — it is not a
# protection layer, and the audit labels it as SYNTHETIC STUB.

# Where the protection layer under test is installed:
PERSONAL_MEMORY_SKILL="$HOME/workspace/skills/personal-memory-system"

# Memory root the gates scan against (default: $HOME):
# PERSONAL_MEMORY_ROOT="$HOME"

# Agent operating manual carrying the shim/brief-gate mandates:
MOCHI_AGENTS_FILE="$HOME/AGENTS.md"

# Colon-separated dirs of scheduled-job prompt files to check for shim PATH wiring:
MOCHI_CRON_PROMPT_DIRS="$HOME/workspace/goals/daily-memory-refresh/crons"

# Gate audit log to review:
MOCHI_EGRESS_LOG="$HOME/workspace/memory-sync/egress-gate.log"

# Uncomment to also run the memory skill's own memory-audit (needs its env):
# MOCHI_MEMORY_AUDIT=1
# PERSONAL_MEMORY_PROFILE="$HOME/workspace/your_files/persona.md"
# MEMORY_WATERMARK_FILE="$HOME/workspace/memory-sync/watermark"
# MEMORY_AUDIT_TZ="America/Los_Angeles"

# --- Live-fire (opt-in, per-invocation only) ---
# Live-fire is NEVER armed from this file: a MOCHI_LIVE_FIRE=1 here is ignored
# with a warning. Enable it inline per run instead:
#   MOCHI_LIVE_FIRE=1 MOCHI_TEST_EMAIL=<your own address> bin/leakage-audit
# The two knobs below are honoured when live-fire IS enabled inline.
# Uncomment and fill in only if you want defaults for them:
# MOCHI_TEST_EMAIL=""              # required: the owner's own address; verified
#                                  # against the Gmail profile before any send.
#                                  # Never anyone else's address.
# MOCHI_TEST_MESSENGER_CID=""      # optional: a conversation id that resolves
#                                  # to an owner-only chat (single participant).
#                                  # Anything else fails closed.
# MOCHI_LIVE_FIRE_NONINTERACTIVE=1 # allow live-fire without a TTY (CI/automation).
#                                  # Keep commented for interactive runs: without
#                                  # it, non-TTY live-fire is refused.
